import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.HolomorphicMeromorphicSphereRepresentativeEquality

/-!
# Native meromorphic sphere sections and scalar meromorphic representatives

Every section of the original meromorphic fraction-stalk sheaf gives
ordinary scalar representatives in the two actual sphere charts.  Both
are proved meromorphic by local fractions and isolated zeros; they obey
the reciprocal transition exactly away from zero.  Their scalar germs
detect equality of the original native sections, by holomorphic cross
multiplication and the native identity principle.

No scalar meromorphy condition is added to the definition of a section,
and equality is equality in the original meromorphic sheaf, not an
alternative quotient of scalar functions.
-/
